      "proof_trace": "The sole token comparison at L30 uses JavaScript's `!==` operator (`if (token !== validToken)`), which short-circuits at the first differing byte and is not constant-time. No `crypto.timingSafeEqual` or equivalent is used anywhere in the codebase, and there is no rate limiting. The proof fails at this line — no constant-time guard exists.",
      "attack_scenario": "An attacker sends repeated HTTP requests to any authenticated endpoint (e.g., `POST /api/roles/sync`) with candidate token prefixes, statistically measuring response latency to identify correct bytes one at a time, eventually reconstructing `API_AUTH_TOKEN` and gaining full API access.",
      "checklist_id": "PROP-stem-bot-v21-inv-001"
    },
    "text": "Token comparison must use constant-time algorithm to prevent timing side-channel extraction.",
    "assertion": "forall req: auth_compare(req.token, valid_token) uses timing_safe_equal, not ===",
    "covers": "SG-002_authMiddleware",
    "severity": "HIGH",
    "type": "invariant"
  }
}

